---
title: Smoked chicken Thai salad
servings: 4
tags: [chicken, smoker]
cuisine: thai
source: Smoked Chicken Thai Salad by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/smoked-chicken-thai-salad
---

> A restaurant recipe: the rub is a large batch; use only what the chicken needs.

== Sweet chili dressing ==

Whisk the @sweet chili sauce{6%tbsp}, @fish sauce{2%tbsp} and @lime juice{2%tbsp}.

== Chicken rub ==

Mix the @ground black pepper{12%tbsp}, @seafood boil seasoning{12%tbsp}(Cajun), @granulated garlic{3%tbsp}, @chicken bouillon{3%tbsp}(granulated) and @kosher salt{7 1/2%tsp}.

== Smoked chicken ==

Heat a #smoker{} to 225°F with post oak.

Pat the @chicken thighs{4} dry and lay them on a #sheet tray{}. Season both sides with the rub and @salt{1%tsp}.

Smoke ~{90%minutes}, until 165°F inside. Cool a little and slice.

== To serve ==

Toss the @cabbage{8%oz}(white, shredded), @Roma tomatoes{1%cup}(halved), @cucumbers{2}(sliced), @mixed greens{}(Asian salad mix), @cilantro{1/2%cup}(micro or small leaves), @mint leaves{1/2%cup}(micro or small leaves), @Thai basil leaves{}(micro or small leaves) and @Asian pear{1}(sliced) with 2 tbsp of the dressing.

Put it in a bowl, lay the chicken on top and scatter over the @fried shallots{1/2%cup}. Serve the rest of the dressing on the side.
